<urn:usf:contract:cli-transition-definition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "Require current ordinary construction evidence, proof and published exact scoped grant before source edits. Require exclusive ownership of shared CLI write scopes. Domain handlers, locks, receipt validators, recovery draft, provider policies and schedulers are read-only except the separately required USF-1195 integration validation process cleanup repair; that exception permits only bounded owned-process/stdio settlement and its focused regressions. The separately required shared binding-declaration reader extraction may move the existing pure Linear binding parser into graph source and reuse it in no-effect context interrogation; dispatch, attempts, receipts, supersession admission, locks and provider behavior remain unchanged. The separately required completion-evidence canonical preparation may extract the existing no-persistence evidence producer and delegate both interfaces to it; all proof, publication and persistence handlers retain their guards. Mutation transition mappings remain explicitly unmapped until separately admitted. The separately required no-change non-destructive replay repair may modify only materialiseNoChangeCandidate and focused regressions to authenticate and reuse exact existing state, preserve/refuse partial or conflicting existing state, and leave all other candidate operations, locks and publication semantics unchanged. The separately required candidate content digest repair may share candidate identity canonicalization between resolver and realisation, treating validated write content as opaque while preserving metadata/path guards and all previously accepted digests; generic provider digest and provider Contribution identity remain unchanged. Resolver errors retain their existing typed classification. The separately required canonical no-change execution extension may share the existing transition kernel across explicitly admitted observation and candidate-workspace effects, separate command-result and produced-artifact schema validation, export the existing native no-change producer with closed request validation, and add canonical CLI delegation and focused tests. It must not change native candidate identity, locks, creation/cleanup/replay semantics, provider behavior, proof, publication or completion authority. Effect admission requires exact compiled rule and recovery-case compatibility; graph declarations alone remain insufficient. The separately required canonical checked-receipt reuse currentness repair may modify src/commands/check.ts and focused regressions to share exact current validation-claim projection between receipt production and read authentication, compare authenticated current candidate facts and complete runtime authority dependency paths/bytes, and reject self-consistently rehashed stale claims before reuse. It must preserve receipt schema and digest domain, native execution, locks, persistence/recovery and integration-specific authority checks. It grants no new check adapter, semantic completion or parallel authority. The separately required root-derived selective check adapter has the additional bounded exception specified in the separate construction constraint." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:contract:cli-transition-definition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "The canonical-operational-support requirement may modify only src/commands/transition.ts, src/graph/cli-transitions.ts and the existing native adapter preflight extraction paths src/collaboration/local-contribution.ts, src/commands/check.ts, src/commands/work-completion.ts and src/realisation/index.ts with focused coverage tests. One atomic candidate may additionally write graph/cli-transition-definition.nq only with the exact declared native, kernel, schema and record targets, current construction authority and exact authenticated preimages; existing integration authority must independently rederive and authenticate postimage bases before primary advancement. The read-only inspector and real producer share a private typed prepare-context; no exported unknown execution context, caller-supplied authority, new seed kernel, independently authored schema, stored state, lock, effect, provider, completion or parallel authority is admitted. The existing interrogation schema may only add a reference to a canonical descriptor generated definition." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:contract:cli-transition-definition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "The completion-proof-publication-recovery-terminal requirement separately extends earlier proof/publication read-only constraints only in src/commands/work-completion.ts, src/realisation/work-completion.ts, src/commands/transition.ts, src/graph/cli-transitions.ts, src/cli.ts, src/commands/help.ts and their declared focused tests. It permits shared native proof/publication extraction, immutable durable publication snapshots and bounded native recovery under the existing primary mutation lock, plus typed terminal authentication using the existing completion evaluator. Existing check.ts and realisation/index.ts are read-only dependencies; no scheduler, provider, controller or parallel authority. Preserve publication receipt and candidate digest domains, exact source postimages and original authenticated lineage. Current construction and exclusive source ownership are required; generated schemas change only through semantic generation and governed publication." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:contract:cli-transition-definition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "The separately required completion-check-receipts execution-intent repair extends the selective-check exception only in src/commands/check.ts and its focused tests, including tests/fixtures/realisation/check-interruption.ts. It may persist, authenticate and reconcile the graph-owned checked-candidate execution intent at the derived existing receipt boundary. Both native entrypoints must refuse retained unknown execution before cleanup or dispatch; legacy explicit behavior remains unchanged only when no intent exists. Preserve the existing candidate lock, scalar receipt schema/digest domain, native receipt publication and confinement. Read the tracked intent schema and validate its required fields and states against current semantic authority. No new scheduler, controller, metrics authority, provider contact, completion or parallel authority is granted." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:contract:cli-transition-definition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "The separately required completion-proof canonical preparation is an exception to earlier proof-handler read-only constraints only for src/commands/work-completion.ts, src/commands/transition.ts, src/cli.ts, src/commands/help.ts, tests/integration/work-completion.test.ts and tests/unit/commands/transition.test.ts. Extract and share the existing no-persistence native proof producer with immutable closed input and post-await currentness readback. Preserve legacy optional persistence, evaluator, proof obligation guards, locks, digest domains, schema files, receipt execution/recovery and publication. Canonical admission must validate the exact nonempty evidence prerequisite and reciprocal consumed-artifact producer; do not erase prerequisite edges or infer satisfaction from ordering. Root-only preparation uses shared native candidate identity and read-only retained-set authentication, never ensure/run checks or repair pending state. Current scoped construction and exclusive shared-file ownership are mandatory. No independent review, new lifecycle, provider contact, publication, terminal or parallel authority is granted." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:contract:cli-transition-definition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "The separately required owned-runtime check recovery extends the selective-check composition exception only in src/realisation/index.ts, src/commands/check.ts, src/commands/work-completion.ts and their already declared focused tests. It may factor existing workspace and receipt authentication into private strict versus exact check-runtime contexts; keep ordinary exported readers strict. Add named check-recovery readers and an authenticated no-change callback under the existing candidate lock, with no caller-supplied runtime paths or ignore flags. Check-local tree projection must authenticate the owned scratch root before exclusion. Native intent preflight may expose its existing authenticated disposition for dynamic recovery ordering. Both native entrypoints preserve unknown outcomes before cleanup; matching current receipt settlement may use existing scratch cleanup followed by ordinary strict readback. Preserve all other inventory, manifest, identity, mode, confinement, receipt schema/digest and lock guards. Tests must cover real retained execution views after SIGKILL, zero duplicate children, wrong scratch type/mode/symlink, unrelated extra entries, and ordinary-reader refusal. No new scheduler, provider, completion, parallel or metrics authority is admitted." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:contract:cli-transition-definition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "The separately required pending receipt-publication snapshot repair may modify only the existing scalar receipt publication and recovery composition in src/commands/check.ts, existing compiled-rule fingerprint compatibility in src/commands/transition.ts, canonical receipt-set observation in src/commands/work-completion.ts, and focused interruption/root regressions. It must share one authenticated publication snapshot between native mutation and named read-only recovery, preserve the ordinary strict receipt reader, update the existing compiled-rule fingerprint compatibility for the amended rule text, and never project pending or hardlinked publication as a current receipt, receipt-set result, evidence, completion or terminal state. It may add no receipt schema or stored state, controller, adapter, lock policy, provider contact, proof, publication or parallel authority." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:contract:cli-transition-definition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "The separately required root-derived selective check adapter may extract the unchanged no-change candidate identity derivation in src/realisation/index.ts, share current-or-absent receipt authentication in src/commands/work-completion.ts, and expose ensure-current-or-run-absent under the existing candidate lock in src/commands/check.ts. It may add only the corresponding graph-compatible adapter, input delegation, result-schema reference validation and help in src/commands/transition.ts, src/cli.ts and src/commands/help.ts with focused regressions. Authenticate all retained required receipts before any missing obligation executes; reread each member under the native lock and reuse current receipts rather than duplicate concurrent execution. Preserve native identity/digest domains, locks, legacy explicit execution, publication and recovery guards. Stable receipt-set identity must exclude invocation-specific execution/reuse observations. Unsafe, stale, unknown or ambiguous state refuses without repair; no new set-atomic recovery, provider, scheduler, proof, publication, semantic completion or parallel authority is granted." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:contract:cli-transition-definition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "The separately required selective-check currentness composition repair may extract the unchanged native authenticated no-change workspace reader into a callback-under-existing-candidate-lock boundary in src/realisation/index.ts and delegate its existing public reader without changing its validation, identity or lock implementation. The complete-set reader in src/commands/work-completion.ts must use that boundary rather than nested lock acquisition. In src/commands/check.ts, pre-spawn reauthentication may use existing shared semantic basis derivation plus exact authenticated raw manifest and complete candidate-fact snapshots after execution-view construction, without calling or weakening the ordinary whole-workspace inventory reader while its owned scratch exists. Focused genuine interruption, drift and complete-set tests may change in the already declared test paths. No new lock policy, scratch exemption, receipt schema, controller, provider, completion or parallel authority is admitted." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:contract:cli-transition-definition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "This additive local-source scope permits only a native local contribution producer and the existing resolver union, with canonical transition registration and tests. Existing domain handlers, publication, locks, provider Contribution identity and metrics semantics remain unchanged except the separately required USF-1195 integration validation process cleanup repair. The shared binding-declaration extraction may replace only the duplicated pure declaration interpretation in the Linear handler. The separately required completion-evidence canonical preparation may extract and share the no-persistence completion evidence producer, add its canonical input delegation, and reauthenticate current scoped authority before returning; existing legacy persistence, proof, publication and recovery guards remain unchanged. Local bytes are not provider success or independent review. Refresh aggregate construction evidence/proof/grant after the amendment; no old scoped grant authorizes newly added paths. The separately required no-change non-destructive replay repair may modify only materialiseNoChangeCandidate and focused regressions to authenticate and reuse exact existing state, preserve/refuse partial or conflicting existing state, and leave all other candidate operations, locks and publication semantics unchanged. The separately required candidate content digest repair may share candidate identity canonicalization between resolver and realisation, treating validated write content as opaque while preserving metadata/path guards and all previously accepted digests; generic provider digest and provider Contribution identity remain unchanged. Resolver errors retain their existing typed classification. The separately required canonical no-change execution extension may share the existing transition kernel across explicitly admitted observation and candidate-workspace effects, separate command-result and produced-artifact schema validation, export the existing native no-change producer with closed request validation, and add canonical CLI delegation and focused tests. It must not change native candidate identity, locks, creation/cleanup/replay semantics, provider behavior, proof, publication or completion authority. Effect admission requires exact compiled rule and recovery-case compatibility; graph declarations alone remain insufficient. The separately required root-derived selective check adapter has the additional bounded exception specified in the separate construction constraint." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
