<urn:usf:requirement:source-bound-terminal-diagnostics:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Extend the existing terminal obligation reader with closed typed diagnostic observations for every refusal. Derive reasonCodes as the deduplicated projection of those diagnostics, never as a competing verdict. Each diagnostic identifies its actual source subject and source-row digest; identify the graph predicate, projected property, governing edge-rule identity and digest, expected target type, scope, and observed IRI targets where known. Missing targets must not acquire invented artifact identities. Required-edge absence must name the source, predicate, rule, expected target type and currentness basis. Preserve distinct same-code failures at different sources or under different rules, deterministic ordering and exact deduplication. Refuse diagnostic overflow beyond 1024 records; do not silently truncate or turn invalid policy declarations into success. Keep all existing structural refusal conditions, terminal artifacts, satisfaction, effect-adapter admission and parallel safety unchanged. Schemas must be generated through the canonical field specifications and the interrogation wrapper must reference them. Tests seed missing downstream evidence/recovery edges, wrong target types/scopes, duplicate same-code failures, source/rule currentness movement, malformed policies and overflow. This diagnostic extension admits no check execution, repair, integration, publication or completion." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
