<urn:usf:rule:completion-publication-reauthentication:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Under the existing primary mutation lock reauthenticate bundles, current scoped authority, exact source preimage and prepared postimage using the existing native publisher. Before source mutation persist and fsync immutable no-follow owner-only snapshots of exact source pre/post bytes, bundle bytes, canonical expected receipt bytes and bounded metadata; fsync directories before effect. Snapshot identities bind original work/profile/manifest, native intent, original scoped basis and full authority dependency denominator. On restart read before normal partial-state rejection, but independently rederive original checked evidence/proof and prepared publication from authenticated preimage view plus unchanged current external dependencies. A serialized basis, schema-valid receipt or self-rehashed snapshot is never authority. Require actual source exactly original preimage or exact prepared postimage and receipt absent or exact matching bytes. Resume only that intent; conflicts, changed authority, unsafe/missing/ambiguous snapshot or unrelated source movement preserve/refuse. Reconcile durable pending snapshot without treating it absent. Before-effect state may perform the original write; exact postimage with absent receipt may create only the exact authenticated prepared receipt; exact postimage plus matching receipt is replay. Never overwrite original lineage, delete historical snapshots or roll back an observed postimage because acknowledgement was lost. Read back source, receipt and native completion evaluator before success. Verify never repairs. Durability covers declared fsync boundaries and genuine SIGKILL, not untested power-loss guarantees." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
