<urn:usf:rule:completion-publication-snapshot-authentication:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "At most one selected publication snapshot per exact selected root/profile/manifest and original native intent; ambiguous historical matches refuse rather than choose newest. Snapshot root derives only from selected policy; no caller path input. Bound records and file inventories, reject symlinks/hardlinks, verify owner/mode and fd/path identity, strict UTF-8 and exact byte lengths. Store exact immutable bytes in no-replace files; digest descriptors bind every file. Validate full closure and source pre/postimage before recording snapshot durable and before mutation. Metadata/files must independently reproduce native authenticated checked evidence, proof, intent and publication receipt; hash integrity is not original authority. Preserve settled and refused history. A root-only invocation must recover without caller-reconstructed bundle or basis." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
