<urn:usf:rule:completion-snapshot-file-source-authentication:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "SnapshotFile.path is always the immutable snapshot-relative file path, validated relative to the selected snapshot root, never an original repository path inferred from a filename convention. Every entry requires byteLength equal to the actual bounded file read and digest over exactly those bytes. Roles authority-input, source-preimage and source-postimage require both sourcePath and sourceMode; sourcePath identifies the original repository-relative source and sourceMode binds actual permission bits 0..511. Roles proof-bundle and expected-receipt must omit sourcePath and sourceMode because bytes are derived rather than copied from an external source file. Independently rederive the exact inventory from the authenticated preimage graph, basis read/runtime/check requirements and member workspace; reject omissions, extras, duplicates, stale mode or bytes, unsafe paths and ambiguous source identity. Only the exact declared source preimage/postimage publication effect is exempt from equality with current source bytes; all other dependencies must still match. Preserve existing 1024-file and 64 MiB total limits and 16 MiB per-file bound. Structural optionality is not permission to omit role-required authority; enforce role rules in the shared native snapshot authenticator, never by generic schema shape alone." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
