<urn:usf:rule:completion-terminal-native-evaluation:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Accept only a fresh native evaluateNoChangeCompletionRecords/deriveWork verified-complete readback for exact selected work/profile/manifest and full completion obligation denominator. Bind actual native realisation receipt, Evidence and ProofResult IRIs, authenticated publication receipt/path/intent, original publication basis and current scoped basis separately, exact source and authority dependency digests and actual evaluator resourceDigest. Refuse stale, ambiguous, partial, unsafe or mismatched lineage; never convert declaration, topology, descriptor schema, copied accepted record or passing deterministic proof alone to accepted. This evaluator covers local no-change completion only, not independent review, live commissioning, entire Linear circuit or parallel proof. Repeat source/receipt/authority currentness readback before acknowledgement. Runtime accepted records must be supplied only by a compiled adapter calling the existing native completion evaluator over freshly loaded actual graph/receipt state. Graph CLI projection must not import command runtime, trust asserted accepted records, or clear unrelated evaluator diagnostics. Check exact evaluator rule digest and typed record basis/source/receipt/member identities again in the command-side adapter before attachment. Generic census remains structural; global satisfaction stays unverified while any required artifact/recovery is unauthenticated. The publication artifact family includes actual realization receipt, Evidence, ProofResult and publication receipt as authenticated native member identities, not invented fixed output IRIs." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
