<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-input:1> <urn:usf:predicate:version> "1" <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-intent:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A readonly preparation invocation has no durable intent mutation. Its proposed operations and selected basis determine the returned local artifact identity; incomplete stdout after interruption is not an artifact and must be discarded." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-intent:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CliFieldDerivationRule> <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-intent:1> <urn:usf:predicate:version> "1" <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-readback:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Parse the closed LocalContribution and rederive exact current basis/preimages before returning it. Bind actual preparation-tool source digest and operation bytes. Unknown original author/model/token/cost remain null; no invocation or review independence is asserted." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-readback:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CliFieldDerivationRule> <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-readback:1> <urn:usf:predicate:version> "1" <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-replay:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "After interruption or unknown/truncated stdout, re-interrogate current authority and repeat readonly preparation. Never apply partial JSON or reuse stale basis. No call-result, provider attempt, lock, receipt or completion record is repaired or manufactured." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-replay:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CliFieldDerivationRule> <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-replay:1> <urn:usf:predicate:version> "1" <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-scope:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Derive current semantic reads and exact file preimages from the selected work/basis and proposed operation paths. Reobserve bounded no-follow source identities before output; refuse unsafe links, file movement, unsupported files and undeclared paths. Empty static scope arrays do not assert that context-derived scopes are empty; operational scope derivation remains mandatory." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-scope:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CliFieldDerivationRule> <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-scope:1> <urn:usf:predicate:version> "1" <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-serial-safety:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Admit one no-effect proposal observation only after the current construction/source/input guards pass. Do not infer parallel safety from this serial admission. The observation returns a proposal or refusal and never applies its operations; downstream effects reauthenticate their own currentness. A concurrent source change may refuse observation and never licenses state repair." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-serial-safety:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CliFieldDerivationRule> <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-serial-safety:1> <urn:usf:predicate:version> "1" <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-terminal:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Local preparation terminates only with a closed structurally valid current proposal or a typed refusal. Its terminal result is not Golden Path completion. Normal downstream validation, review, integration and completion/reconciliation obligations remain required." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-terminal:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CliFieldDerivationRule> <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:local-preparation-terminal:1> <urn:usf:predicate:version> "1" <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-guard:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Existing native materialisation requires exact current active construction authority and valid graph-selected no-change policy. Authenticate source scope, policy and basis again under the existing candidate lock. Missing, stale or ambiguous authority refuses; descriptor availability is not eligibility." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-guard:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CliFieldDerivationRule> <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-guard:1> <urn:usf:predicate:version> "1" <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-input:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Canonical intended request contains only rootIdentity and manifestPath. Derive unique work/contract/profile through the shared context resolver, then derive the exact work packet, current immutable basis and graph-selected no-change completion policy. Candidate digest, workspace, policy, basis, profile and work overrides refuse. The canonical --input adapter may delegate only to the shared native no-change producer after exact compiled admission; the legacy explicit parser remains a compatibility interface. A binding root is refused until separately implemented, never guessed." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-input:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CliFieldDerivationRule> <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-input:1> <urn:usf:predicate:version> "1" <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-readback:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Authenticate exact manifest identity, current scoped basis, full expected workspace inventory and bytes before returning a workspace result. Existing complete matching state is reused without deletion or rewriting. Candidate existence, empty operations and successful return establish neither validation nor completion." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-readback:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CliFieldDerivationRule> <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-readback:1> <urn:usf:predicate:version> "1" <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-replay:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A fresh absent workspace may be created after current authority authentication. If interrupted before any workspace effect, absence must be observed again before retry. If effect completed but acknowledgement was lost, restart reauthenticates and reuses the exact complete workspace. Abrupt partial creation, unsafe/missing manifest, conflicting bytes, stale relevant basis or unknown state refuse without deleting retained state. Caught fresh-creation errors use existing bounded cleanup, which is not crash atomicity or power-loss durability. No partial-workspace repair or automatic outcome assumption is admitted." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-replay:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CliFieldDerivationRule> <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
