<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-scope:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Existing native effect may create only the derived private no-change candidate workspace and existing per-candidate operational lock state. Primary repository source, Git, provider, evidence/proof, publication and Linear state are untouched. The candidate identity is derived from current basis, policy, empty operations/lineage, scope, write set and exact preimages." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-scope:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CliFieldDerivationRule> <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-scope:1> <urn:usf:predicate:version> "1" <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-terminal:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A successful no-change workspace is only input to all graph-required completion checks. Check/review/evidence/proof/publication/reconciliation obligations remain separately required; no terminal satisfaction or execution authority follows from this producer descriptor." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
